<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Layout xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE <Layout>
         breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent
         xml file" error.

         BUSINESS FIELDS ADDED 2026-08-20 (UAT gap). Until now this layout was a STUB: it carried
         exactly four fields, Name, OwnerId, CreatedById and LastModifiedById, and not one business
         field. Clicking "Add Broker Response" on the BOV Outreach stage therefore opened a "New BOV
         Submission" modal offering only a blank auto number and an Owner picker, so the analyst had
         nowhere to type the broker, the amount, or the terms.

         WHY IT SURVIVED TO UAT: every read path bypasses layouts. BovSubmissionSelector names its
         columns in SOQL and bovComparisonMatrix renders them itself, so the matrix looked complete
         while the create and detail screens were empty. A layout is only exercised by the standard
         create and detail UI, and nothing in the Jest or Apex suites touches it.

         🔴 A SECOND EXPOSURE THIS CLOSES, AND ONE UAT STEP IT NEEDS.
         lwc/bovComparisonMatrix/bovComparisonMatrix.js handleAddResponse navigates to
         standard__objectPage actionName 'new' with encodeDefaultFieldValues({ Disposition__c }) -
         and Disposition__c WAS NOT ON THIS LAYOUT. The create screen renders its inputs from this
         layout, so there was no input for that default to land in, and the analyst could not have
         set the parent by hand either.
         ⚠ WHETHER THE PLATFORM STILL APPLIES A DEFAULT TO A FIELD WITH NO RENDERED INPUT IS NOT
         STATED IN THE defaultFieldValues DOCUMENTATION, AND WAS NOT TESTED HERE. So this is
         recorded as an open risk, not as a finding: if the value was being dropped, every
         submission created through that button is orphaned from its Disposition and existing UAT
         data needs checking. Placing Disposition__c here removes the question either way.
         CONFIRM IN UAT: create one submission through "Add Broker Response" and check the parent
         is populated. Do not assume it was, and do not assume it was not.

         BEHAVIOUR RULES APPLIED, and each Readonly below is deliberate:
         1. FORMULA FIELDS CANNOT BE EDITABLE. Broker_Display__c, Property_Name__c and
            Selected_Broker__c are formulas (verified in objects/BOV_Submission__c/fields/); a
            formula carrying behavior=Edit fails the deploy outright.
         2. MACHINE WRITTEN FIELDS ARE Readonly. Approval_Status__c is written ONLY by
            workflows/BOV_Submission__c.workflow_meta Set_Broker_Approval_Approved and
            Set_Broker_Approval_Rejected, fired as the final actions of
            approvalProcesses/BOV_Submission__c.Broker_Finalize_Approval. A hand edit would make the
            field disagree with the approval that owns it, and BovSubmissionTriggerHandler reads
            exactly that value to advance the parent Disposition from BOV Outreach to Broker
            Selection. Editing it by hand would move a deal without an approval. This is the same
            reasoning that set Selected_Broker__c to readonly on the Disposition FlexiPage
            yesterday under code review W1, and it is applied consistently here.
            It also MATCHES THE FLS ALREADY IN THE ORG: permissionsets/DPEG_Disposition_Edit grants
            Approval_Status__c readable=true editable=false, so an Edit behaviour here would have
            advertised a write the persona does not have.
         3. Name stays Readonly. It is an AutoNumber, displayFormat BOV-{0000}.
         4. Submission_Status__c IS LEFT EDITABLE ON PURPOSE. It is the team's own pick, set by
            hand or by BovSubmissionService.replaceSelectedBroker, and it is a different field from
            Approval_Status__c: the trigger requires BOTH. BOV_Score__c is likewise left editable,
            because nothing in Apex or Flow writes it, only reads it for the ORDER BY.

         THE relatedLists BLOCK BELOW IS UNTOUCHED. It carries RelatedProcessHistoryList, which is
         the only route to Recall Approval Request on this object.

         =================================================================================
         REVISED 2026-08-20. THE BROKER PICK BECOMES A LOOKUP, AND SIX FIELDS LEAVE THIS PAGE.
         =================================================================================
         🔴 EVERY REMOVAL BELOW IS DISPLAY ONLY. NOT ONE FIELD IS RETIRED FROM THE SCHEMA, NOT
         ONE IS RENAMED, AND NO FLS IS REVOKED. A field absent from a layout is still queried,
         still written by Apex, still readable in reports and list views, and still granted by
         permissionsets/DPEG_Disposition_Edit and DPEG_Disposition_View. Everything that read
         these fields yesterday reads them unchanged today.

         1. ADDED TO Information: Broker__c, labelled "Broker Contact", a Lookup to Contact with
            an ACTIVE non-optional filter on Is_Broker__c. behavior=Edit is legal because it is a
            Lookup. It is now THE ONLY BROKER ENTRY POINT ON THIS PAGE.
            ⚠ It renders as a type ahead search box, not a fixed list combobox. That is the
            confirmed decision, so do not raise it in UAT as a defect.

         2. REMOVED FROM Information: Broker_Firm__c and Contact_Name__c.
            WHY: they are no longer typed. BovSubmissionBrokerStampService stamps both in before context
            from the Contact chosen in Broker__c, so an editable input for either would offer
            the analyst a value the next save overwrites. The user asked not to see or enter
            them. They REMAIN STORED Text fields and REMAIN POPULATED, which is what keeps
            BovSubmissionTriggerHandler's approval stamp onto Disposition__c.Selected_Broker__c,
            BovSubmissionService.replaceSelectedBroker, the Broker_Display__c formula,
            BovController.BovRow and the bovComparisonMatrix and backupBrokers columns working
            with zero code change.

         3. DELETED ENTIRELY: the "Broker Selection and Approval" section, carrying
            Broker_Display__c, Property_Name__c, Selected_Broker__c and Approval_Status__c.
            WHY THIS CHANGES NO BEHAVIOUR: all four were Readonly here and none is human
            written. Broker_Display__c, Property_Name__c and Selected_Broker__c are FORMULAS
            (they recompute regardless of any layout), and Approval_Status__c is written only by
            the Set_Broker_Approval_Approved and Set_Broker_Approval_Rejected workflow field
            updates fired by Broker_Finalize_Approval. Hiding a formula does not stop it
            evaluating and hiding a workflow written field does not stop the workflow.
            ⚠ Approval_Status__c REMAINS the field BovSubmissionTriggerHandler reads to advance
            the parent Disposition from BOV Outreach to Broker Selection. That path is untouched
            and must still be regression tested after this deploy.
            ⚠ Disposition_Dashboard_Access still grants Broker_Display__c, Property_Name__c and
            Selected_Broker__c read; that set is deliberately NOT edited by this change.

         4. UNCHANGED: BOV Terms, System Information, the CustomLinks section, and the
            relatedLists block. 🔴 THE relatedLists BLOCK IS LOAD BEARING, SEE ITS OWN COMMENT
            BELOW: it carries RelatedProcessHistoryList, which is Approval History, and this
            object has no FlexiPage, so deleting it would strand every submitted BOV with no
            route to Recall Approval Request. It survived this edit verbatim. -->

    <layoutSections>
        <customLabel>false</customLabel>
        <detailHeading>false</detailHeading>
        <editHeading>true</editHeading>
        <label>Information</label>
        <layoutColumns>
            <layoutItems>
                <behavior>Readonly</behavior>
